## Minimal session restoration probe

The following scratch-only source ran with `node /workspace/scratch/500c5aa1eb33/v34/session-reset-probe.mjs > /workspace/scratch/500c5aa1eb33/v34/session-reset-probe.log 2>&1`. It creates and closes one independent disposable local engine, uses no application state or network and reproduces only the fixture restoration behavior. The two suite engine instances also close as before.

```js
import { PGlite } from '/workspace/scratch/205dbad31641/p5-sql-work/environment/node_modules/@electric-sql/pglite/dist/index.js';
const db=await PGlite.create();
const who=async(label)=>console.log(label,(await db.query('SELECT session_user,current_user')).rows);
try {
 await db.exec('CREATE ROLE anon NOLOGIN; CREATE ROLE service_role NOLOGIN;');
 await who('initial');
 for (const sql of [
  'BEGIN;', 'SET LOCAL SESSION AUTHORIZATION anon;', 'SET LOCAL ROLE service_role;', 'ROLLBACK;', 'RESET SESSION AUTHORIZATION;', 'RESET ROLE;', 'SET SESSION AUTHORIZATION postgres;', 'RESET ROLE;'
 ]) {try {await db.exec(sql); console.log(sql,'ok');}catch(e){console.log(sql,e.message,e.code)};try{await who('after')}catch(e){console.log('who',e.message)}}
}finally {await db.close();}
```

After the attempted nonmember SET ROLE returns 42501, the log records anon/anon after ROLLBACK, RESET SESSION AUTHORIZATION and RESET ROLE. Explicit SET SESSION AUTHORIZATION postgres then restores postgres/postgres. This is observed local engine behavior, not a claim about supported deployed session handling.

## Limits

PGlite 0.5.12/PostgreSQL 18.6 uses one serialized connection, fictional Auth/approval/policy and controlled local clock/response hooks. Actual local SQL role/ACL, crypto and transport behavior does not establish supported deployed Auth, current policy, native multi-backend concurrency, synchronous revocation, HTTP fault injection, trusted provider finality or device acceptance. All 21 native cases remain unrun. Catalog pass is a metadata observation with `deployable:false`; it neither authenticates function bodies nor proves host routing, quiescence or draining already-running legacy calls. No connected SQL/settings, actual Auth/provider/model/voice call, paid edit, participant activation or publication occurred. V2 remains inactive/nondeployable.

